.TH STORMBYTE-GITHUB 1 "August 2026" "StormByte" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
StormByte-GitHub \- unified CLI for managing StormByte GitHub repositories, Actions caches, CI runs, submodules, dumps, releases and sanitizer tests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B StormByte-GitHub
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B StormByte-GitHub
is a convenience wrapper around common Git and GitHub operations used in the StormByte project ecosystem.
It provides a consistent interface for managing Actions caches, CI workflow runs, submodules, repository synchronisation, forks, local repository listings, source code dumps, version releases and AddressSanitizer / ThreadSanitizer test builds across multiple local clones.

The script requires a mandatory configuration file
.I ~/.StormByte-GitHub.conf
containing at least the variables
.BR OWNER ,
.BR ROOT
and
.BR OUT .
.B FORK_ROOT
is optional.
If the file does not exist on first run, the script interactively prompts for the values (with short explanations and path completion where applicable), validates them and writes the configuration.
Empty optional values (such as
.BR FORK_ROOT )
are omitted from the file.

.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I ~/.StormByte-GitHub.conf
Configuration file. Supported variables:
.RS
.TP
.B OWNER
GitHub username that owns the repositories. Used to verify origin remotes and for
.BR clone-all .
.TP
.B ROOT
Working root directory that contains local repository clones. Used by most commands when no explicit path is given, and by
.BR "repos list" .
.TP
.B OUT
Output directory used by
.B repos dump
(created automatically if missing).
.TP
.B FORK_ROOT
Optional root used
.B only
by the
.B fork
commands. If unset, fork uses
.BR ROOT .
.RE

.SH GLOBAL ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
Any of the configuration values can be overridden for a single run via the environment (same idea as
.BR DRY_RUN ):
.TP
.B DRY_RUN=1
Simulate actions without applying any changes.
.TP
.B ROOT=\fI/path\fR
Override
.B ROOT
from the config file for this run.
.TP
.B OUT=\fI/path\fR
Override
.B OUT
from the config file for this run.
.TP
.B OWNER=\fIname\fR
Override
.B OWNER
from the config file for this run.
.TP
.B FORK_ROOT=\fI/path\fR
Override
.B FORK_ROOT
from the config file for this run.
.TP
.B PAGE_LIMIT=\fIN\fR
Items per API page (default: 100).
.TP
.B MAX_PAGES=\fIN\fR
Maximum number of cache-delete passes (0 = until empty).
.TP
.B RUN_LIMIT=\fIN\fR
Maximum number of workflows to re-run (0 = all).
.TP
.B ONLY_FAILED=1
Legacy equivalent of the
.B --failed
flag.

.SH DIRECTORY SELECTION
Most commands accept an optional directory specification. The argument is always a
.B local directory
(where the repository is cloned), not the GitHub repository name.
.TP
(no argument)
Operate on every immediate subdirectory of the effective root
.RB ( ROOT
for most commands;
.B FORK_ROOT
or
.B ROOT
for
.BR fork ).
.TP
.B <dir>
Operate only on that directory. May be absolute, relative,
.BR ~/... ,
or a simple name resolved as
.IR <root>/<name> .
.TP
.B !<name>
Operate on all directories under the effective root except the named one.
.TP
.B !<name1>+!<name2>+...
Operate on all directories under the effective root except the listed names.

Notes:
.IP \(bu 2
A concrete path (~/…, /…, ./…, foo/bar) is used as-is.
.IP \(bu 2
A simple name is resolved as
.IR <root>/<name> .
.IP \(bu 2
The root is
.B ROOT
for most commands, and
.B FORK_ROOT
(or
.BR ROOT )
for
.BR fork .
.IP \(bu 2
The argument is always a local directory (clone path), not the GitHub repo name.
.IP \(bu 2
When using
.B !
exclusions from an interactive shell, quote them with single quotes
(e.g.
.BR "'!multimedia'" )
to avoid Bash history expansion.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS help
.TP
.B help
Show the built-in help message and exit.

.SS cache
.TP
.B cache show\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--name\fR \fIpattern\fR]
List each Actions cache (size, id, key) per repository together with totals.
With
.B --name
only caches whose key matches the glob pattern are shown.
.TP
.B cache list\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--name\fR \fIpattern\fR]
Show a compact summary of cache count and size per repository.
With
.B --name
only caches whose key matches the glob pattern are counted.
.TP
.B cache delete\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--name\fR \fIpattern\fR]
Delete Actions caches (paginated until none remain).
With
.B --name
only caches whose key matches the glob pattern are deleted.
Respects
.BR DRY_RUN .
.PP
The
.B --name
pattern uses bash glob syntax (e.g.
.BR '*ccache*' ,
.BR 'sccache-Windows-*' ,
.BR '*v1-release*' ).
The flag may appear in any position after the subcommand.

.SS ci
.TP
.B ci stop\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Cancel all active workflow runs on the current branch.
.TP
.B ci start\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--failed\fR]
Re-run the latest finished run of each workflow. With
.B --failed
only failed / cancelled / timed-out runs are re-launched.
.TP
.B ci restart\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--failed\fR]
Equivalent to
.B ci stop
followed by
.BR "ci start" .
.TP
.B ci status\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Show a summary of recent workflow runs.

.SS submodules
.TP
.B submodules init\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Initialize and checkout submodules recursively.
.TP
.B submodules deinit\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Deinitialize all submodules.
.TP
.B submodules update\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Clean, fetch, update submodules to the remote tip and commit/push if necessary.
When no directory is specified the update is performed in dependency order
(using a topological sort over
.BR ROOT ).
.TP
.B submodules list\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
List submodule entries from
.I .gitmodules
for each selected repository: name, path and URL.
If a repository has no submodules, a neutral informational message is shown
(not treated as an error or warning).
.TP
.B submodules add \fI<dir>\fR \fI<URL>\fR \fI<path>\fR \fB--name\fR \fI<name>\fR
Add a new submodule to a single repository.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.I <dir>
is the local clone (bare name under
.BR ROOT ,
or an absolute /
.BR ~/ /
relative path; may lie outside
.BR ROOT ).
.IP \(bu 2
.B --name
is required and may appear in any argument position. Use quotes when the name contains spaces; the quotes are not part of the stored name.
.IP \(bu 2
.I <path>
must be relative to the selected repository. Absolute paths and any path containing
.B ..
are rejected.
.IP \(bu 2
Runs
.B git submodule add --name ...
only; does
.B not
run submodule init or update afterwards.
.IP \(bu 2
Respects
.BR DRY_RUN .
.RE
.TP
.B submodules delete \fI<dir>\fR (\fB--name\fR \fI<name>\fR | \fB--url\fR \fI<url>\fR | \fB--path\fR \fI<path>\fR)
Remove one submodule from a single repository.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Exactly one of
.BR --name ,
.B --url
or
.B --path
is required (flags may appear in any position).
.IP \(bu 2
.B --path
must be relative to the repository (no absolute path, no
.BR .. ).
.IP \(bu 2
Cleans the submodule from the index and
.IR .gitmodules ,
then deletes the submodule directory on disk (even if it has local changes).
.IP \(bu 2
Does
.B not
commit and does
.B not
push, so the change can be reviewed and undone with
.B git reset --hard
if needed.
.IP \(bu 2
Respects
.BR DRY_RUN .
.RE

.SS git
.TP
.B git reset\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Hard-reset and clean the working tree of the selected repositories.
.TP
.B git pull\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Fetch and pull with rebase (does not touch submodules).
.TP
.B git sync\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Alias for
.BR "git pull" .

.SS repos
.TP
.B repos list
List every immediate subdirectory of
.B ROOT
(non-recursive). For each folder the following columns are shown:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
folder name
.IP \(bu 2
remote repository (
.IR owner/name )
.IP \(bu 2
latest tag (version-sorted), or short commit hash if there are no tags
.IP \(bu 2
current branch
.RE
Non-git directories are listed with placeholders.
.TP
.B repos dump \fI<directory>\fR [\fIchunk_size_kb\fR] [\fBtype=c++\fR|\fBtype=cmake\fR]
Concatenate source files of a project into one or more text files under
.BR OUT .
Optionally split the result into chunks of the given size.
A bare directory name is resolved under
.BR ROOT ;
absolute and
.B ~/
paths are used as given.
.TP
.B repos status\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Report the state of the
.B current branch
in each selected repository under
.BR ROOT :
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B OK
— working tree clean and no unpushed commits relative to the upstream tracking branch
.IP \(bu 2
.B DIRTY
— uncommitted changes in the working tree
.IP \(bu 2
.B UNPUSHED
— local commits not present on the upstream (or no upstream configured)
.IP \(bu 2
.B DIRTY+UNPUSHED
— both of the above
.RE
Does not run
.BR fetch ;
ahead/behind reflect the last known upstream tips.
.TP
.B repos push\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Run
.B git push
on each selected repository under
.BR ROOT
.B without
.B --force
or
.BR --force-with-lease .
Repositories with no upstream tracking branch are skipped with a warning.
Failures are reported per repository without aborting the whole batch.
Respects
.BR DRY_RUN .
.TP
.B repos release \fR[\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fIversion\fR] [\fB--list\fR | \fB--delete\fR | \fB--skip-ci\fR]
Create, list or delete version tags and GitHub Releases for repositories under
.BR ROOT .
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.I <dir>
/
.I dir-spec
is a local clone (bare name under
.BR ROOT ,
absolute /
.BR ~/ /
relative path, or exclusion syntax
.BR !name ,
.BR !a+!b ).
.IP \(bu 2
.I <version>
must be valid SEMVER when used for create/delete (optional leading
.BR v ,
optional pre-release/build suffix), e.g.
.BR 1.0.0 ,
.BR v1.0.0 ,
.BR 1.0.0-rc.1 .
.IP \(bu 2
The repository remote must belong to the configured
.BR OWNER
(for every selected repo).
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive confirmation (
.B yes
) is required for create and delete. There is no non-interactive override flag.
.IP \(bu 2
Respects
.B DRY_RUN
for create and delete.
.RE
.PP
.B List
.RB ( --list )
— directory and version are optional:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Lists
.B GitHub Releases
(via
.BR "gh release list" ),
not plain tags as the primary table.
.IP \(bu 2
Directory selection follows the same rules as other commands: all under
.BR ROOT ,
a single directory, or
.B !
exclusions.
.IP \(bu 2
If
.I version
is omitted, every release is shown. If
.I version
is given, only matching releases are shown.
.IP \(bu 2
Positional parsing with
.BR --list :
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
(no positionals) — all repos, all releases
.IP \(bu 2
.I <dir-spec>
— selected repos, all releases
.IP \(bu 2
.I <version>
— all repos, that version only (argument must look like SEMVER)
.IP \(bu 2
.I <dir-spec> <version>
— selected repos, that version only
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Tags that exist locally or on
.B origin
without a matching GitHub Release are reported as a
.B friendly note
(not an error).
.IP \(bu 2
.B --delete
and
.B --skip-ci
are ignored with a warning when combined with
.BR --list .
.RE
.PP
.B Delete
.RB ( --delete )
— requires
.I <dir>
and
.IR <version> :
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Removes the GitHub Release (if present) and the git tag locally and on
.BR origin .
.IP \(bu 2
Does not require a clean tree, CHANGELOG, or a specific branch.
.IP \(bu 2
.B --skip-ci
is ignored with a warning.
.IP \(bu 2
If neither the release nor the tag exists, the command succeeds as a no-op with a warning.
.RE
.PP
.B Create
(default, without
.B --list
or
.BR --delete )
— requires
.I <dir>
and
.IR <version> :
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
The current branch must be
.B master
or
.B main
and the working tree must be clean.
.IP \(bu 2
.I CHANGELOG.md
must exist at the repository root and contain a non-empty section for
.I <version>
whose header matches
.B "## [<version>] - YYYY-MM-DD"
(optional
.B v
inside the brackets; example:
.BR "## [1.0.0] - 2026-08-20" ).
The section body is used as the GitHub Release notes.
.IP \(bu 2
Before tagging, the script fetches and pulls with rebase, then
.B waits for CI
on the current commit to be green (all workflow runs completed with success/skipped/neutral), unless
.B --skip-ci
is passed. Waiting can take a long time;
.B Ctrl-C
during the wait aborts cleanly with
.B no tag created yet
.
.IP \(bu 2
If the new version is
.B older
(SEMVER core) than the latest existing tag, the command fails.
If it is the
.B same
core version as an existing tag, or if the tag/release already exists, the existing GitHub Release and tag are
.B deleted and recreated
.
.IP \(bu 2
Versions containing
.B -
(e.g.
.BR 1.0.0-rc.1 )
are published with
.B gh --prerelease
.
.IP \(bu 2
Sequence on success: confirm → fetch/pull → optional CI wait → optional delete old tag/release → annotated tag → push branch → push tag →
.B gh release create
.
.RE

.SS test
.TP
.B test asan\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fIoptions\fR...]
.TP
.B test tsan\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fIoptions\fR...]
Build and run AddressSanitizer (asan) or ThreadSanitizer (tsan) tests for the selected repositories.
Directory selection follows the same rules as other multi-repo commands
(all under
.BR ROOT ,
a single directory, absolute /
.BR ~/ /
relative paths, or
.B !
exclusions).

For each repository the script:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Creates a temporary build directory (default
.B build-asan
or
.BR build-tsan ).
If the directory already exists the repository is skipped with an error (safety).
.IP \(bu 2
Configures the project with CMake, injecting the appropriate
.B -fsanitize=...
flags
.B before
any user-supplied
.BR --cmake-options
(so the user can override them).
.IP \(bu 2
Compiles with
.BR "cmake --build ... -j$(nproc)" .
.IP \(bu 2
Runs the tests according to the priority below.
.IP \(bu 2
Always removes the build directory at the end (success or failure) via a trap.
.RE

A report file is written
.B only when an error occurs
and contains solely the output of the test execution (ctest or the direct binary).
The path of the generated report is announced explicitly.

.PP
.B Options
.RS
.TP
.B --builddir \fIDIR\fR
Build directory relative to the repository root
(default:
.B build-asan
/
.BR build-tsan ).
.TP
.B --testdir \fIDIR\fR
Directory passed to
.B ctest --test-dir
(default:
.IR $builddir/test ).
.TP
.B --outfile \fIFILE\fR
Report file path
(default:
.IR /tmp/<repo>_asan_report.txt
or
.IR /tmp/<repo>_tsan_report.txt ).
Written only on error.
.TP
.B --cmake-options \fI"opts"\fR
Extra arguments passed to
.B cmake
after the sanitizer flags (the user can therefore override them).
The string is expanded correctly so that
.B cmake
does not see a single quoted argument.
.TP
.B --executable \fIPATH\fR
Run this binary directly instead of
.BR ctest .
The path may be absolute or relative to the build directory.
.TP
.B --test \fIREGEX\fR
Run
.B ctest -R REGEX
instead of all tests.
Ignored when
.B --executable
is also present.
.TP
.B --asan-options \fI"opts"\fR
Value for the
.B ASAN_OPTIONS
environment variable (only meaningful with
.BR asan ).
Default:
.BR abort_on_error=1:halt_on_error=1:detect_leaks=1:symbolize=1:print_stacktrace=1 .
.TP
.B --tsan-options \fI"opts"\fR
Value for the
.B TSAN_OPTIONS
environment variable (only meaningful with
.BR tsan ).
Default:
.BR abort_on_error=1:halt_on_error=1:symbolize=1:print_stacktrace=1 .
.TP
.B --verbose
Show the full output of the CMake configure and compile steps.
Without this flag only a one-line progress indicator is shown
.RB ( "Configuring ASAN … OK" ,
etc.).
.RE

.PP
.B Execution priority
(per repository)
.RS
.IP 1. 3
.B --executable
→ run the binary directly
.IP 2. 3
.B --test
→
.B ctest -R REGEX
.IP 3. 3
(none) →
.B ctest
(all tests)
.RE

.SS Other commands
.TP
.B clone-all
Clone every public repository belonging to
.B OWNER
that is not already present under
.BR ROOT .
.TP
.B search \fI<text>\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Search for the given text inside the selected repositories. Matching terms are highlighted when the terminal supports colour.
.TP
.B fork status\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Uses
.B FORK_ROOT
if set, otherwise
.BR ROOT .
Show whether a repository is a fork and, if so, how many commits it is behind / ahead of its upstream.
.TP
.B fork sync\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Uses
.B FORK_ROOT
if set, otherwise
.BR ROOT .
Synchronise
.B only the master branch
with the upstream repository when the fork is behind. Forks that are already up to date are skipped. The current branch is preserved and any local changes are safely stashed.
.TP
.B fork branch-status\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Uses
.B FORK_ROOT
if set, otherwise
.BR ROOT .
For each selected repository, list every local branch other than
.B master
and report whether merging that branch into
.B master
would be conflict-free, using
.B git merge-tree
(read-only):
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B CLEAN
/
.B CONFLICTS
.IP \(bu 2
Local-only branches are annotated
.B local-only (not pushed)
.
.IP \(bu 2
No local branches other than
.B master
→ neutral message, success.
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# First run – interactive configuration
StormByte-GitHub help

# List local clones under ROOT
StormByte-GitHub repos list

# Working tree / unpushed status
StormByte-GitHub repos status
StormByte-GitHub repos status crypto

# Push current branch (no force)
StormByte-GitHub repos push

# List GitHub Releases (optional dir-spec / version)
StormByte-GitHub repos release --list
StormByte-GitHub repos release database --list
StormByte-GitHub repos release '!multimedia' --list
StormByte-GitHub repos release --list 1.0.0
StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0 --list

# Tag + GitHub Release (CHANGELOG section must match <version>; confirm with "yes")
StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0
StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0 --skip-ci
DRY_RUN=1 StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0

# Delete tag + GitHub Release (confirm with "yes")
StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0 --delete
DRY_RUN=1 StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0 --delete

# Fork helpers
FORK_ROOT=~/Forks StormByte-GitHub fork status
FORK_ROOT=~/Forks StormByte-GitHub fork sync
FORK_ROOT=~/Forks StormByte-GitHub fork branch-status

# Caches / CI
StormByte-GitHub cache list
StormByte-GitHub cache list --name '*ccache*'
StormByte-GitHub cache show multimedia --name 'sccache-Windows-*'
StormByte-GitHub cache delete '!multimedia'
StormByte-GitHub cache delete --name '*v1-release-msvc*'
StormByte-GitHub ci start --failed

# Git / submodules
ROOT=~/Software StormByte-GitHub git sync
StormByte-GitHub submodules update
StormByte-GitHub submodules list crypto

# Search / dump
StormByte-GitHub search "mimalloc"
StormByte-GitHub repos dump ./base type=cmake 200

# Sanitizer tests
StormByte-GitHub test asan
StormByte-GitHub test asan multimedia
StormByte-GitHub test tsan '!multimedia'
StormByte-GitHub test asan database --cmake-options "-DENABLE_FOO=ON" --verbose
StormByte-GitHub test asan multimedia --executable bin/my_test --outfile /tmp/report.txt
StormByte-GitHub test tsan crypto --test "Thread.*"
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error (invalid arguments, missing configuration, git/gh failure, CI red, aborted confirmation, sanitizer test failure, etc.)

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.StormByte-GitHub.conf
Configuration file (OWNER, ROOT, OUT; optional FORK_ROOT).
.TP
.I functions.sh
Shared helpers (logging, SEMVER, version_plain, topological sort, \ldots).
Looked for first next to the script, then in
.IR /lib/StormByte/ .
.TP
.I git.sh
Git-specific helpers. Same search path as
.IR functions.sh .

.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Repositories must belong to the configured
.B OWNER
(or
.B OWNER
env override).
.IP \(bu 2
Omitting the dir-spec walks every immediate subdirectory of the effective root.
.IP \(bu 2
Running with no arguments shows the built-in help.

